      "side": 1,
      "message": "We should explore allocating this structure based on the devicetree.    \n\nOne potential model to follow could be the subsys/net.  Network drivers install using NET_DEVICE_INIT(), instead of DEVICE_INIT(), which handles allocating the private structures for the driver, and allocating a \"struct net_if\" in the subsystem.\n\nThe net_if also supports referencing the network interface by \"struct net_if *iface\" or by an index.  This also seems like a good model to follow.",
      "range": {
